# Title -> name entry ("A", confirmed) -> main menu -> Volume, and the wheel turned while the
# page is up: two clicks one way, a click and two the other, then back out. The level the wheel
# sets is what this measures, against the pure recompilation (tests/vs-recomp.sh): the two
# level pages read the wheel's slots directly, unlike the menus, and for a long time read the
# wrong one — the slider never moved, and no other script turns the wheel on either page.
200: select
300: wheel +240
400: wheel +240
500: wheel +24
800: select
1100: select
1500: select
2000: wheel +8
2400: select
2900: wheel +8
3100: shot
3200: wheel +8
3600: wheel -8
3800: shot
3900: wheel -16
4300: shot
4600: menu
5200: quit
